        en: 'Allergic rhinitis (hay fever, persistent runny/blocked nose) is present in 60-80% of people with asthma \u2014 the "one airway, one disease" concept. Treating the nose well (saline rinses, intranasal steroid) measurably improves asthma control. Ask about morning sneezing, blocked nose, postnasal drip \u2014 and treat them as part of asthma management, not a separate problem.',
